      "reasoning": "*strokes chin thoughtfully*\n\
\n\
AH! The time for combat has arrived! Let me assess my dark forces!\n\
\n\
**EMPEROR OF BONES** stands ready! A magnificent 2/2 skeletal ruler!\n\
\n\
**GRAN-GRAN** suffers from summoning sickness and cannot attack this turn!\n\
\n\
*ominous music plays*\n\
\n\
My opponents have two **RUIN CRABS** - each mill 3 cards when they or a creature you control deal combat damage to a player!\n\
\n\
*wicked grin*\n\
\n\
If I attack, those crabs will mill 3 cards from MY graveyard! Do they contain my precious **PSYCHIC FROG**?! My **GRAN-GRAN**?! My **ABHORRENT OCULUS**?!\n\
\n\
*counts cards*\n\
\n\
I have 19 cards in my graveyard - plenty of fodder! But the crabs will keep milling throughout combat...\n\
\n\
*mysterious cackle*\n\
\n\
Let me study the battlefield more carefully... I have **EMPEROR OF BONES** who targets opponents' graveyards, not mine! And my **PSYCHIC FROG** is safe in exile!\n\
\n\
But still... two crabs milling 3 cards each = 6 cards potentially stripped from my dark collection!\n\
\n\
*strokes chin*\n\
\n\
The safer play: **DEFEND**! Hold my Emperor back and let the opponent attack! My Emperor can then exile MORE cards from their graveyard!\n\
\n\
*ominous music plays*\n\
\n\
I PASS ON ATTACKING! Let them come to me!\n\
