      "decision_index": 19,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Surgical Extraction on Ragavan is a poor target choice. The opponent's graveyard contains Persist (2 copies), which is the key reanimation spell that could bring back Archon of Cruelty (also in their graveyard). Archon of Cruelty is an 8-mana 6/6 flyer that generates massive value on ETB. The opponent has a Swamp in play and Persist costs only 1B - they could reanimate Archon as early as next turn. Ragavan is a 1-drop creature that is much less threatening, especially since the opponent is clearly on a reanimation strategy. Alternatively, extracting Psychic Frog (2 copies in graveyard) would remove a key threat that could be Unearthed or Persisted back cheaply. But Persist is the most critical target since removing it prevents the opponent from cheating Archon of Cruelty into play.",
      "action_taken": "Targeted Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer with Surgical Extraction",
      "better_line": "Target Persist with Surgical Extraction to remove both copies from the opponent's graveyard, preventing them from reanimating Archon of Cruelty or any other creature from their stacked graveyard.",
      "type": "blunder",
