    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Emperor of Bones exiled Ragavan (2/1) instead of Abhorrent Oculus (5/5 flyer with manifest dread). When Emperor adapts for {1}{B}, it puts the exiled creature onto the battlefield - getting a 5/5 flyer is dramatically better than a 2/1. The player's reasoning about exiling from the opponent's graveyard was also confused since Ragavan was in their own graveyard.",
      "action_taken": "Exiled Ragavan, Nimble Pilferer (2/1) with Emperor of Bones' trigger",
      "better_line": "Exile Abhorrent Oculus (5/5 flyer) to set up a much more powerful reanimation when Emperor of Bones adapts",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 54,
      "player": "MiniMx Villain",
      "decision_index": 43,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "MiniMx Villain has 3 untapped lands (Swamp, Watery Grave, Island) plus Gran-Gran on the battlefield. Playing Raucous Theater (which enters tapped) before casting spells means they can't use it this turn anyway, but the sequencing issue is that they should cast Psychic Frog first (costs UB) before playing the land. With Gran-Gran's tap trigger providing card filtering, and Psychic Frog being a critical threat that can start growing and pressuring the mill player, deploying Frog immediately is more important. More critically, playing the tapped land triggers both Ruin Crabs, milling 6 more cards from their library when they're already heavily milled (36 cards in graveyard). They should cast Psychic Frog first with their available mana, then play Raucous Theater, since the land enters tapped anyway and doesn't help with mana this turn. Playing the land first gives the opponent free mill triggers before establishing their threat.",
      "action_taken": "Played Raucous Theater before casting any spells, triggering two Ruin Crabs to mill 6 cards.",
      "better_line": "Cast Psychic Frog (UB) first using Watery Grave + Island or Swamp, then play Raucous Theater and cast Unearth to reanimate Emperor of Bones or another creature. The land enters tapped regardless, so sequencing spells first loses nothing and delays giving free mill triggers.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 64,
      "player": "MiniMx Villain",
      "decision_index": 54,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Spent 3 mana on Faithless Looting flashback for card filtering when already holding strong cards and clear deployment lines. The opponent has multiple Ruin Crabs + Hedron Crab actively milling, so MiniMx needs to deploy threats quickly rather than spend mana filtering. They already have reanimation targets in graveyard and Unearth/Emperor of Bones to use them.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Faithless Looting from graveyard for {2}{R} flashback, using 3 of 4 available mana on card filtering.",
      "better_line": "Deploy threats immediately: Cast Emperor of Bones ({1}{B}) + Psychic Frog ({U}{B}) for 4 mana total, putting two creatures on board to pressure the mill player. Or cast Unearth ({B}) on a graveyard creature + Psychic Frog ({U}{B}) leaving mana for Emperor of Bones, maximizing board presence against the clock.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 75,
      "player": "MiniMx Villain",
      "decision_index": 65,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarding Faithless Looting as the first of two discards is fine since it can be flashed back, but the key question is what the second discard will be. However, looking at this specific choice in isolation: Faithless Looting is a reasonable discard since it has flashback and can be cast again from the graveyard. The real consideration is whether discarding an Archon of Cruelty would be better, since the player has Unearth and Persist available to reanimate it. Discarding an Archon + using Unearth (which costs only {B}) to put a 6/6 flying Archon into play would be a much stronger line than keeping both Archons in hand where they cost 8 mana each. Faithless Looting from the graveyard costs {2}{R} and the player has no red source on board, making it nearly useless.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Faithless Looting (first discard selection)",
      "better_line": "Discard an Archon of Cruelty to set up reanimation with Unearth ({B}) or Persist ({1}{B}), which would put a 6/6 flyer with a devastating ETB trigger onto the battlefield for minimal mana. Faithless Looting without red mana available from graveyard is low value anyway, but an Archon in the graveyard enables a game-winning play.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 76,
      "player": "MiniMx Villain",
      "decision_index": 65,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Attacking with 0/2 and 0/3 mill crabs into an opponent with a 1/2 Gran-Gran available to block accomplishes nothing meaningful. The crabs deal 0 damage and are purely defensive/utility creatures whose value comes from landfall mill triggers, not combat. Attacking risks losing a crab to a combat trick or removal during combat, and gains absolutely nothing since they deal 0 damage.",
      "action_taken": "Declared all crabs (Ruin Crab x2, Hedron Crab) as attackers",
      "better_line": "Don't attack with any creatures. The crabs have 0 power and serve no purpose in combat. Keep them back as potential blockers against Gran-Gran or future threats.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 82,
      "player": "Llama4 Spike",
      "decision_index": 75,
    }
  ],
